# Documents.
#
# An allow-list, inverted.
#
# This was `docs/*` with a list of exceptions, and the exceptions fell behind:
# the PRD, the FRD, the technical design, the data model, the delivery roadmap
# and the backend spec sat on disk, invisible to git, for the whole of phase 1.
# Edits to them looked saved and were never committed, because `git status`
# says nothing about a file it has been told to ignore.
#
# That is the fourth time an allow-list has quietly swallowed something in this
# codebase — the others were a required document, an ADR, and a screenshot
# directory. So it is the other way round now: everything under `docs/` is
# tracked, and the few things that genuinely should not be are named.
#
# `scripts/doc-check.sh` asserts that every `.md` under `docs/` is tracked, not
# only the required ones. That is the half that catches the next one.
docs/**/*.tmp
docs/.DS_Store
docs/screens/.sheet.html

# The screens PDF is ten megabytes of the same captures that sit beside it in
# `docs/screens/`, rebuilt by `scripts/build-screens-pdf.py` in a few seconds.
# Committing it would put a new ten-megabyte blob in history every time a colour
# changed.
docs/Keys-screens.pdf

# Build output.
#
# Seventy-five files of Next.js build cache — webpack packs, manifests, chunk
# maps — were committed by a `git add -A` because nothing ignored them and
# nothing checked. `make repo-check` now fails on any of these being tracked,
# which is the half that catches it next time.
.next/
**/.next/
dist/
build/
DerivedData/

# OS / editors
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
*.log

# Node / React Native
node_modules/
.expo/
*.jsbundle
ios/Pods/
ios/build/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
.env
.env.local

# CI is tracked; the `docs/*` allow-list above does not reach it.
!.github/

# Build output and task cache
dist/
.turbo/
*.tsbuildinfo

# .NET
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
*.user

# React Native
apps/mobile/ios/Pods/
apps/mobile/ios/build/
apps/mobile/ios/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
apps/mobile/android/.gradle/
apps/mobile/android/build/
apps/mobile/android/app/build/
apps/mobile/.xcode.env.local

# Gradle and Xcode output from *any* module, not only the app's.
#
# A gitignore pattern containing a slash is anchored to the file it is written
# in, so every `android/build/` rule above matches the repository root and
# nothing else. `packages/tracking-native` is also an Android module, and 168
# of its `.dex` files, class files and transform caches were committed — 1.3 MB
# of build output that `git status` reported as clean, because tracked files
# are not untracked files. Unanchored, so the next native module is covered
# before it exists.
**/android/build/
**/android/.gradle/
**/ios/build/

# Local development tokens and the log of the server that seeded them. Both are
# written by `make round-trip`, both die with that process, and neither belongs
# anywhere near a commit.
.dev-tokens.json
.round-trip-server.log
.round-trip-server.pid

# Engineering standards for whoever is working in here, agent or person.
# Kept out of the published repository; the ADRs carry the reasoning that is
# meant to be read from outside.
CLAUDE.md

# The native projects, generated by `@react-native-community/cli init` and then
# adjusted for this monorepo. The projects themselves are committed — they carry
# the bundle identifier, the permissions and the build settings, and
# regenerating them would silently discard all three. What is ignored is
# everything a build or `pod install` writes back into them.
apps/mobile/ios/Pods/
apps/mobile/ios/.xcode.env.local
apps/mobile/ios/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
apps/mobile/android/local.properties
apps/mobile/android/.cxx/
**/*.xcuserstate
**/DerivedData/
**/*.hprof

# Signing material. A keystore in a public repository is a signing key anybody
# can publish an update to your app with.
*.keystore
!**/debug.keystore
